{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/787963-how-good-is-the-c-td-line-as-a-whole","id":787963,"title":"How good is the C:tD line, as a whole?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-17T03:32:07-08:00","id":787963,"title":"How good is the C:tD line, as a whole?","content":"Now with the C20 kickstarter in full swing, I have been entertaining the thought of backing at a level that includes the entire classic book line (as PDFs). It's quite a deal ($160 vs $270 for the bundle on Drivethru, compared to $450, if you bought all the books individually). How would you rate the entire line as a whole?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5402-malcolmlittle","name":"MalcolmLittle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5402_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T04:14:13-08:00","id":787977,"title":"","content":"I'd do it. The first edition is more closely tied to Celtic myth, in general, and is full colour. The tone generally matches the artwork, with a focus on lost magic, secret places and mythical treasures hidden behind a World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> The later supplements branch out a fair bit and go into many of the darker elements--especially post-Reckoning. The focus turns more to the War in Concordia and in the Dreaming, the rise of the Fomorians, and the class conflict between commoners and nobles. Some people didn't like the Reckoning metaplot, but for Changeling it added some of the best kiths (Adhene) and plot developments, while still allowing for the earlier themes.<br /> <br /> In short, just do it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T09:23:26-08:00","id":788152,"title":"","content":"While I'm still missing some books from the Changeling stuff, in my opinion is an interesting line, surprisingly coherent.<br /> Beside the last supplement (the Changeling section in Time of Judgement), I think they're globally very whorty. (If you can, grab the novels of Immortal Eyes, or you'll need a lot of crossreferences when you'll read the related supplement books).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px;